Notebook[{
Cell["InfraPoint", "Title",ExpressionUUID->"0c44a567-c143-4117-a290-5c8508ff6f41"],

Cell["[LLM Generated]", "Subtitle",ExpressionUUID->"eab49220-9f17-4a0f-9d47-b6c2565a8995"],

Cell["\<\
InfraPoint[{v1, ..., vk}] is the unweighted multi-realisation form (each \
vertex mass 1); InfraPoint[{v1, ...}, {w1, ...}] carries explicit per-vertex \
mass. The canonical form has a duplicate-free support with positive masses \
that add on aggregation; an all-ones weighted form collapses to the bare \
1-arg form. Accessors [\"Support\"], [\"Weights\"], [\"Mass\"], [\"First\"], \
and the graph-keyed synthetic invariants [\"BallVolumes\", g], \
[\"ShellAreas\", g], [\"LogDifferenceQuotients\", g], [\"Dimension\", g], \
[\"ScalarCurvature\", g], [\"CurvatureByRadius\", g] (one result per support \
vertex; extra args forward, e.g. [\"BallVolumes\", g, {0, R}]); the \
Infrageometry primitives also accept the wrapper directly (BallVolumes[g, p] \
== p[\"BallVolumes\", g]). Find* finders return a List of unary \
InfraPoint[{v}] wrappers; wrap with InfraPoint @ ... to collapse via \
auto-flatten (masses add). Scene-language variants InfraPoint[] / InfraPoint[\
\"Center\"] / InfraPoint[\"Periphery\"] / InfraPoint[origin, dist] / \
InfraPoint[n] are constructors used inside InfraScene. In InfraSceneHighlight \
a weighted InfraPoint renders as a mass heat-map (heaviest vertex brightest).\
\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"f18d820a-2615-49c7-bec4-d28330bc9627"],

Cell["Setup", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"85b72d12-3aaf-4282-8739-3a8a520e4429"],

Cell["Load the paclet.", "CodeText",ExpressionUUID->"e52636c9-0905-45e7-a264-4694f8507333"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Needs", "[", "\"\<WolframInstitute`SyntheticInfrageometry`\>\"", 
  "]"}]], "Code",
 InitializationCell->
  True,ExpressionUUID->"e5adb072-e9a0-458b-84b5-4853b530363e"],

Cell["Related Guides", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"ed8f5d53-002c-490c-b277-aa8bb6475974"],

Cell["EuclideanGeometryGuide", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"18dc28ff-65c8-4ac4-9236-35dd3904e9af"],

Cell["SyntheticInfrageometryGuide", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"a7be7884-4bd5-4644-9c2f-2fb3a57791cc"]
},
